# CR 708.7, 701.40b: a manifested creature card may be turned face up for its mana cost, a special action that a creature
# losing all abilities keeps. Unable to Scream on it is the one thing that stops it ("can't be turned face up"). Abhorrent
# Oculus (the opening of the other manifest scenarios) manifests Snapcaster Mage on Bot2's upkeep. On turn 3 the Aura makes
# the face-down 2/2 a 0/2 artifact creature, a Toy (a face-down permanent has no subtypes), and Bot1, with Island's and
# Sol Ring's {C}{C}{U} in its pool for the {1}{U}, is offered no turn-up. Bot2's Wheel of Fortune hand is Disenchant and two Moxen: its
# Disenchant destroys the Aura on turn 4; on turn 5 the same {1}{U} turns it up: Snapcaster Mage, a 2/1 with flash, no
# longer a Toy. (A morph or disguise permanent under the Aura is not turned up for that cost by the Aura's "loses all
# abilities" already: face up it would have no such cost, CR 702.37e, 702.168d.)

